  "provenance": "TMS6100-Emulator (simoninns): a dump of an Acorn PHROM A made with HxD, held in this repository as the capture firmware's firmware/src/romdata_acorn.h until commit c537c1d, and not redistributed since: the image is read from a local copy (MAME's cm62024.bin). The word names are from its word list, whose addresses and numbers all match the image's pointer table. Four of its names contradict the names stored in the image (stored_name) and are corrected from them (listed_as keeps the list's).",
  "word_numbers": "the BBC Micro's word numbers (SOUND -1, <number>, 0, 0): word N's pointer is at byte 2N. Numbers 32-126 (aliases) are the 'ASCII associated' words, which repeat words numbered from 127 on.",
